      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, high room humidity can prevent the ink from bonding properly, causing random faded patches, especially with polyester blends. Additionally, how the paper is handled—such as bending it too sharply while loading—can create gaps that let air get between the transfer and fabric before the heat fuses them. Try using fresh, low-moisture paper and ensuring it is handled minimally to eliminate these micro-pockets.",
