      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The color likely vanishing indicates your heat settings are exceeding the safe temperature limit for that specific fiber blend, causing the ink to over-run or lift off rather than bleed in. Dust or press oil residue on the platen between runs can act as a barrier, preventing localized heat transfer and creating these random voids. I recommend performing a fiber melt test on the blend to find the absolute maximum safe temperature, and flipping the press platen to check for uneven heating zones.",
